  <h1>Projects</h1>
  <p>
    This page lists public work only. Historical game-server systems I took part in are not published here as standalone repositories, so they are not given project links.
  </p>

  <article class="card">
    <h2>pokerBlock</h2>
    <p class="meta">Learning · 2020 · JavaScript</p>
    <p>
      A small program that uses a card-game score sheet to show a hash chain and a difficulty target. It was a way to make a block concrete. It is not a blockchain system.
    </p>
    <p>
      I wrote the demo in one pass: block linking, SHA-256, and a nonce loop. There is no network, no persistence, and no claim beyond the example.
    </p>
    <p><a href="https://github.com/wuyingzhen/pokerBlock">github.com/wuyingzhen/pokerBlock</a></p>
  </article>

  <article class="card">
    <h2>What is not listed</h2>
    <p>
      Forks with no changes of mine, empty repositories, and private work are omitted. A ROS 2 simulation exercise exists, and it is still private because perception and voice are not implemented. It will be linked if it becomes a public project.
    </p>
  </article>
